            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 78-year-old female admitted on 25/03/2014 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and antibiotic cover. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement in oxygenation and symptoms. She was discharged on 26/03/2014 in stable condition. Outpatient follow-up with pulmonology is recommended, along with optimisation of her inhaler regimen and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
